@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] freebsd-candidate-installation
The candidate assembler MUST use a scratch copy of the pinned GPT/UFS image and
immutable installation media. Both installation and kernel verification boots
MUST have no network, bounded execution and clean guest poweroff. The second boot
MUST run without installation media and verify the compiled kernel build token,
the installed kernel digest, root-owned expectation and complete native payload.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;verification] freebsd-candidate-admission
An assembled candidate MAY publish exact disk and kernel provenance, but MUST
retain nativeAdmission=false and distinguish installed files and kernel boot
from Firecracker transport, service, isolation, recovery and catalog acceptance.
Test-only extra root files and runtime hooks MUST NOT enter the default image.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] freebsd-native-sudo-installation
The assembler MUST restore set-ID mode only on the regular, root-owned
`/usr/local/bin/sudo` whose bytes match the pinned verified package closure.
The second boot MUST verify its digest, ownership and exact mode 4755. The stock
sshd service MUST remain disabled so the managed Lyra SSH listener owns port 22.
The reviewed regular, root-owned sudoers policy MUST receive exact mode 0440.
